
              *******************************************
              Scripts for Execution of Standard BOSS Jobs
              *******************************************

All except Conversion Utilities function as

xACTION moleculename

where the BOSS Z-matrix file moleculename.z must be in the current directory.
Output goes to the files out (printed output),
sum (summary file) and plt.pdb (PDB file of final structure).

 Script                   Action
---------     ------------------------------------------------------------------
xOPT        - optimization using the OPLS-AA force field with BFGS optimizer
xOPTF       - optimization using the OPLS-AA force field with Fletcher-Powell
              (faster than BFGS, but not as precise; recommended for complexes)
xOPTP       - optimization using the OPLS-AA force field with Powell
              (try with flat surfaces, e.g. hydrogen-bonded complexes)
xOPT1       - xOPT but optimizes the structure for rc0 (lambda) = 1.0
xOPTUA      - optimization using the OPLS-UA force field with BFGS optimizer
xFREQ       - perform BFGS optimization followed by normal mode calculation;
              uses a frequency cutoff of 500 cm-1, T = 25 C, P = 1 atm
xSP         - single-point force field calculation
xSPM        - xSP, but prepare output plt.pdb and sum (Z-matrix) files for input
              to MCPRO; sum and plt.pdb files use the same unique atom names.
xPDBMCP     - take pdb file to Z-matrix for MCPRO ligand with no optimization of
              structure with CM1A charges and OPLS-AA atom types assigned.

Include polarization:
xPOPT       - optimization using the OPLS-AAP force field with BFGS optimizer
xPOPTF      - optimization using the OPLS-AAP force field with Fletcher-Powell

GB/SA Aqueous Solvation Model:
xOPTGB      - xOPT with GB/SA (BFGS optimizer)
xOPTFGB     - xOPTF with GB/SA (Fletcher-Powell) - recommended
xAM1GBOPT   - xAM1OPT with GB/SA (uses 1.07*CM1 charges)
xPM3GBOPT   - xPM3OPT with GB/SA (uses 1.07*CM1 charges)
xPDGGBOPT   - xPDGOPT with GB/SA (uses 1.07*CM3 charges)

xSPGB       - xSP with GB/SA - uses charges as specified in the Z-matrix
xAM107GB    - xSP with GB/SA - uses 1.07*CM1A charges - yields best
              estimate of deltaG hydration for a neutral molecule

xCSGB100    - xCS100 including GB/SA hydration model
xCSGB200    - xCS200 including GB/SA hydration model
xCSGB500    - xCS500 including GB/SA hydration model
xMCGB       - xMCGAS with GB/SA solvation; MC for solutes in GB/SA solvent
dih*cmd     - see the dihdrive test job for dihedral driving with GB/SA
scan*cmd    - see the scan test job for potential surface scanning with GB/SA

Conformational Search:
xCS100      - MC conformational search with 100 starting structures 
xCS200      - MC conformational search with 200 starting structures
xCS500      - MC conformational search with 500 starting structures
xCS100F     - MC CS with 100 starting structures - (high resolution-
xCS200F     - MC CS with 200 starting structures - may get duplicate 
xCS500F     - MC CS with 500 starting structures - minima)
xSS100      - stochastic conformational search with 100 starting structures
xSS200      - stochastic conformational search with 200 starting structures
xSS500      - stochastic conformational search with 500 starting structures
xSS100F     - stochastic CS with 100 starting structures - high resolution
xSS200F     - stochastic CS with 200 starting structures - high resolution
xSS500F     - stochastic CS with 500 starting structures - high resolution
              note: output structures are in plt.mol with xCS and xSS scripts.
xCSINFO     - utility: list energies of found conformers in csout
xCSMOL      - utility: create separate .mol files for each conformer; they
              can then be displayed individually with, e.g., RasMol
xCSZ        - utility: create separate .z files for each conformer
xGETE       - utility: get Total Energy from first line of Z-matrix file; append
              to energy.CSV; requires full file name, e.g., xGETE molecule.z

Semiempirical Quantum Calculations:
xAM1SP      - AM1 single-point calculation for a neutral system;
              output CM1A charges are scaled by 1.14; usual choice  -
              see boss/notes/CMcharges.
xAM1SP07    - AM1 single-point calculation for a neutral system; output
              CM1A charges are scaled by 1.07; for optimal GB/SA calculations
xAM1SPL     - AM1 single-point for a neutral system; output CM1A-LBCC charges
xAM1SP+     - AM1 single-point for a cation - output charges are unscaled
xAM1SP-     - AM1 single-point for an anion - output charges are unscaled
xAM1SP2-    - AM1 single-point for a dianion- output charges are unscaled
xPM3SP      - PM3 single-point for a neutral system;
              output CM1P charges are scaled by 1.30; see boss/notes/CMcharges.
xPM3SP+     - PM3 single-point calculation for an cation
xPM3SP-     - PM3 single-point calculation for an anion
xAM1OPT     - AM1 optimization for a  neutral system
xAM1OPTL    - AM1 optimization for a  neutral system; output CM1A-LBCC charges
xAM1OPT+    - AM1 optimization for a  cation
xAM1OPT-    - AM1 optimization for an anion
xAM1OPT2-   - AM1 optimization for a  dianion
xPM3OPT     - PM3 optimization for a  neutral system
xPM3OPT+    - PM3 optimization for a  cation
xPM3OPT-    - PM3 optimization for an anion

xAM1CM1     - AM1 single-point calculation for a neutral system;
              output CM1A charges are scaled by 1.00
xAM1CM3     - AM1 single-point calculation for a neutral system;
              output CM3A charges are scaled by 1.00
xPM3CM3     - PM3 single-point calculation for a neutral system;
              output CM3P charges are scaled by 1.00

xPDGSP      - PDDG/PM3 single-point for a neutral system; output
              CM3P charges are scaled by 1.08; see boss/notes/CMcharges.
xPDGSP+     - PDDG/PM3 single-point for a cation
xPDGSP-     - PDDG/PM3 single-point for an anion
xPDGOPT     - PDDG/PM3  optimization for a neutral system
xPDGOPT+    - PDDG/PM3  optimization for a cation - output charges are unscaled
xPDGOPT-    - PDDG/PM3  optimization for an anion - output charges are unscaled
xMDGOPT     - PDDG/MNDO optimization for a neutral system

OPLS/CM1A:
xZCM1A      - convert BOSS Z-matrix file to optimized Z-matrix 
              with 1.14*CM1A charges
xZCM1AL     - same, but output 1.14*CM1A-LBCC charges
xZCM1A+     - xZCM1A for a cation -  output 1.0*CM1A charges
xZCM1A-     - xZCM1A for an anion -  output 1.0*CM1A charges

Monte Carlo Simulations:
xBOX        - execute standard MC simulation for solutes in periodic cube 
              with 500 TIP4P waters at 25 C and 1 atm;
               cutoffs are at 9.0 A with ICUT = 5
xBOX725     - same as xBOX, but use 725 water molecules; 
              both run MC job in background.
xLRCMP      - MC linear response calculation with subsequent properties
              predictions; use scaled CM1P charges; molecule is in drugs
xLRCMPup    - xLRCMP and update a comma-separated file with the results summary
xLRCMPhere  - xLRCMP; molecule is in current directory
xLR725CMA   - execute MC/LR using 725 water molecules and scaled CM1A charges;
              molecule is in drugs directory
xLRAA       - execute MC linear response calculation with subsequent properties
              predictions; use OPLS-AA charges; molecule is in small directory
              -- See testjobs/linres for more information on LR calculations --

xMCGAS      - execute standard gas-phase MC calculation at 25 C

Standard X to Y FEP Calculations:
xFEPGAS     - standard gas-phase FEP calculation at 25 C, 10 windows
xFEPAQ      - standard aqueous FEP: 25 C, 1 atm, 500 TIP4P waters, 10 windows
xFEPAQQ     - queue version of xFEPAQ - see testjobs/FEPaq/PhXtoY
xFEPAQ725   - standard aqueous FEP: 25 C, 1 atm, 725 TIP4P waters, 10 windows
xFEPCAP     - standard aqueous FEP: 25 C, 1 atm, 22-A TIP4P cap, 10 windows
xSOSGAS11   - overlap sampling FEP as for xFEPGAS, 11 windows
xSOSAQ11    - overlap sampling FEP as for xFEPAQ, 11 windows
xSOSAQQ11   - queue version of xSOSAQ11
xFEPCLN     - clean-up FEP directory
xSUMDELG    - extract deltaG results from sum files (for DW-FEP)
xDELGSOS    - sum DeltaGs from FEP SOS calculation
xSUMDW      - sum DeltaGs from double-wide FEP calculation
              See the FEPaq and SOSaq test jobs for more information 
              on these FEP calculations.
xZQFEP      - prepare Z-matrix for charge annihilation FEP calculation
xZLJFEP     - prepare Z-matrix for Lennard-Jones annihilation FEP calculation

Conversion and Display Utilities:
x           - display PDB file with Rasmol (usage: x filename)
xPDB        - convert Z-matrix file to PDB file and display with Rasmol
xRAS        - display structure in plt.pdb with Rasmol 
xNEAR       - trim large PDB file to focus on region around specified residue(s)

xPDBZ       - convert PDB file to optimized BOSS Z-matrix for neutral system
xPDBZ+      - same as xPDBZ except for cation
xPDBZ-      - same as xPDBZ except for anion
xZmol       - convert Z-matrix file to MDL mol file; creates moleculename.mol
xZPDB       - convert BOSS Z-matrix file to PDB file; creates moleculename.pdb

xMOLZ       - convert MDL .mol file to optimized BOSS Z-matrix file for neutral
xMOLZ+      - same as xMOLZ except for cation
xMOLZ-      - same as xMOLZ except for anion
xMOLPDB     - convert MDL .mol file to PDB file
xMOLZnob    - xMOLZ except bond lengths are not optimized (reduce # variables)
xMOL2Z      - convert .mol2 file to optimized BOSS Z-matrix file
xGJFZ       - convert Gaussian job file to optimized BOSS Z-matrix file 
              for neutral molecule
xTOUNIX     - convert MS-DOS text files to UNIX format 
              (e.g., remove ^M at end-of-line)
xADDH       - take pdb file, add hydrogens, and output new pdb

Other Scripts:
xMANY       - utility to run a script on a list of files (xMANY filelist script)
              - this is very useful.

xPARGEN     - run the pargen program to interactively generate a BOSS par file

xQPROP      - execute QikProp for properties predictions; input BOSS Z-matrix,
              MDL mol, mol2, or a PDB file. Need to give full file name, e.g.,
              xQPROP sustiv.mol
              QikProp is solely distributed by Schrodinger Inc.
xQPCON      - combines QikProp output with BOSS conformational search output
              to yield conformationally averaged QikProp predictions.
xQS         - execute the QikSim program for similarity analyses.
xBM         - execute the BOMB program for the generation of analogs or a
              combinatorial library.
              Note: the BOMB program is distributed separately from BOSS.
---------     ------------------------------------------------------------------

Note: not all of the scripts use the latest version of the par file format.
Some entries may be missing; they are not needed for the script. See 
boss/par.form for the latest, complete version.
